 "comment": "Beethoven string quartet (Grosse Fuge / Op. 131 spirit): the same interpretation as the Beethoven piano version. Timing (tempo, rubato, fermatas, breaths, humanise), dynamics and roles are copied unchanged from performance/beethoven_piano/plan.json (sha256 022c22e645321fc1, commit 27b7fc0); read its _interpretation for the reading. What changes for four bowed players is the voicing: the piano brings entries out by hammer velocity (role_boost), the strings by bow pressure and timbre, so every role of the piano plan gets a role_level on the CC1/CC11 envelope in proportion to its velocity boost (+12 velocity is about one dynamic step): subject and answer +1.0, the apotheosis tune +1.1 (piano +14), cf and the major answer +0.7 (+9), the pivot's sigh (melody) +0.5 (+6), the liquidation heads +0.4 (+5, so Climax I stays below Climax II), subject tails and countersubjects +0.2 (+3), free voices -0.3 (-5). role_boost is kept (perform.py halves it for strings: the attack bite). Pedal spans are the piano's and are ignored by the strings. Everything specific to the quartet (the viola hand-off, balance trims, sforzandi, articulation, the deeper swells, hall) is in quartet.json and render.sh.",
